# Build output. The binary is compiled from source and never committed: a
# tracked binary is rewritten by every build, so a clean worktree turns dirty
# on a command that changed no source at all, and the diff is megabytes of
# noise that hides the change the commit is actually about.
/arxi-tui
/arxi-tui.exe
# The whole bin/ tree is build output, so ignore the directory rather than
# enumerating each artifact. Enumerating them is what let bin/arxi-tui.exe~ — an
# editor/build backup the exact-path patterns did not match — get committed as a
# 4.9 MB tracked binary, the precise failure this comment warns about.
/bin/
# Release artifacts from scripts/build-release.sh. Same reason as the binary
# above: cross-compiled output rewritten on every release build, never a source
# of truth, so it is produced into dist/ and published to GitHub Releases rather
# than committed.
/dist/
# Local agent coordination state (writer lock + append-only log). Per-machine
# runtime scratch, never a source of truth, so it stays out of the repo.
/.arxi/

# A stray `go build` inside core/cmd/arxi leaves the binary next to the source.
/core/cmd/arxi/arxi
/core/cmd/arxi/arxi.exe
/core/arxi
/core/arxi.exe
/arxi
/arxi.exe
/arxi.exe.new
/arxi.new
